descriptions.job-1kj6k7d:
&lt;h3&gt;About the Position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a strategic and collaborative Workplace Services and Experience APAC Lead to head our workplace services (WS) functions across Hong Kong and Singapore. This is a senior leadership role focused less on deep technical subject-matter expertise—we already have strong expertise on the ground—and more on providing the vision, people leadership and connective tissue that lets our APAC teams thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll set the strategic direction for WS across the region, mentor and develop a growing multi-office team, and act as the primary conduit between APAC and our colleagues in London and New York. You&#39;ll bring a calm, collaborative leadership style, set a high bar for service, and help our APAC offices feel like a coherent part of the global Jane Street experience while still reflecting their local context.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your areas of focus will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setting the strategic direction for our Workplace Services and Experience team across Hong Kong, Singapore and our growing footprint in the region, in close partnership with global WS leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building, mentoring and motivating a multi-office team spanning our Operations, Food and Front of House teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as the primary conduit between our APAC WS teams and our London and New York counterparts, ensuring alignment, knowledge-sharing and consistent global standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading vendor strategy across the region: sourcing, selecting, partnering with and managing third-party providers (catering, cleaning and others) to deliver excellent service and value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the build-out and opening of new APAC spaces as our footprint grows, partnering with our Engineering, IT and other internal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning regional WS budgets and using financial data to make sound operational decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Championing Jane Street&#39;s culture across the region, making sure visitors feel welcome and Streeters feel happy, engaged and well supported&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipating and resolving workplace issues proactively, and shaping how WS evolves as our APAC operation grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role involves regular travel between our APAC offices. Ideally, you’ll also be willing to spend extended periods embedded in our New York and London offices in your first year to build relationships with global counterparts and ground yourself in how the team operates across the firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significantly experienced leading workplace services, hospitality, office management or a closely related function (ideally across multiple sites and/or markets)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong people manager first and foremost: someone who has built, developed and motivated teams, is comfortable leading through other managers, and can bring out the best in people across different cultural contexts; You set clear expectations, give and invite direct feedback&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic thinker with vision: you are able to set direction, prioritise across competing demands and turn ideas into operational reality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a track record of building strategic vendor partnerships, underpinned by strong financial acumen: you are skilled at selecting the right partners, cultivating long-term relationships and bringing out the best in suppliers to deliver excellent service across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural conduit, collaborator, and strong communicator: you are skilled at building trust across regions and functions, and at translating between local context and global priorities, with excellent people skills and a genuine hospitality mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in a flat, fast-moving environment with little hierarchy; you thrive on ambiguity and change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Having familiarity with the APAC market and an existing personal network of hospitality/workplace services professionals across the region is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English; fluency in additional regional languages (Cantonese, Mandarin) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you&#39;re a recruiting agency and want to partner with us, please reach out to agency-partnerships@janestreet.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

descriptions.job-1kv3nk9:
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Product Marketing team’s mission is to generate customer insights that inform Stripe’s product strategy, and lead go-to-market for our suite of products. Product Marketing is a highly cross-functional role at Stripe, partnering closely with Product and Engineering, Sales, Partnerships, Demand Generation and Campaigns to name a few. Different from many other Product Marketing teams, our team works across the entire product lifecycle, from helping shape the product, to driving launch and commercialization, to growing product adoption post-launch. We also drive both self-serve and sales-sold marketing efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking a product marketer to drive the end-to-end GTM strategy and execution for Radar. As a Product Marketing Manager, you will shape the product roadmap, own product-level messaging and positioning, create differentiated content for events and presentations, support product launches, and enable sales. Reporting to the Fraud and Risk PMM Lead, you’ll partner with product and sales teams to drive awareness and adoption in a rapidly evolving market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an early strategic partner on new offerings — shaping product direction, defining target segments, and building the GTM foundation (positioning, packaging, pricing narrative) from zero to one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive end-to-end product launches, including define audience segments, gather user insights, craft launch narratives, inform pricing and packaging, ensure cross-functional readiness, and execute launch activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop differentiated messaging and positioning, equip GTM teams with knowledge and content to sell and market effectively &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create high-impact thought leadership content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with product, sales, data science, pricing and cross-functional marketing teams to identify new opportunities to drive awareness, demand, and adoption of our products and build the right marketing strategies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product marketing or growth marketing experience at a technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with experience translating technical features into benefits for a technical audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of working cross-functionally across product, sales, and growth teams to drive business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-1ckkll5:
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2 ace-line old-record-id-doxlgpANLHz7HX19U7y9uqLN1Vi&quot;&gt;Who We Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-doxlgo7jwmMifT6u81wqiQARfIh&quot;&gt;At OKX, we believe that the future will be reshaped by crypto, and ultimately contribute to every individual&#39;s freedom.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-doxlgeMS7sZKE7eHvVFBHuWF1gb&quot;&gt;OKX is a leading crypto exchange, and the developer of OKX Wallet, giving millions access to crypto trading and decentralized crypto applications (dApps). OKX is also a trusted brand by hundreds of large institutions seeking access to crypto markets. We are safe and reliable, backed by our Proof of Reserves.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-doxlgSXBYoV9mhnlW7Mw54m5WRe&quot;&gt;Across our multiple offices globally, we are united by our core principles: &lt;em&gt;We Before Me&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Do the Right Thing&lt;/em&gt;, and &lt;em&gt;Get Things Done&lt;/em&gt;. These shared values drive our culture, shape our processes, and foster a friendly, rewarding, and diverse environment for every OK-er.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-doxlgmPYQR4PRXaCxJk9hwWzumb&quot;&gt;OKX is part of OKG, a group that brings the value of Blockchain to users around the world, through our leading products OKX, OKX Wallet, OKLink and more.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2 ace-line old-record-id-doxlgt6ix2u2qGGGvfQF70MEtte&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-doxlgLREN2x6vnVLhX70ZQYkG9g&quot;&gt;This is a sales and account management role focused on VIP retail clients in the CIS region. You will own a portfolio of high-value trading accounts — building relationships, driving VIP upgrades, and actively prospecting new clients to grow OKX&#39;s presence in the region. Working closely with regional growth, product, and business intelligence teams, you&#39;ll be the on-the-ground point of contact for CIS-based VIP traders, combining strong client servicing with a proactive sales approach.&lt;/div&gt;
